# SSH connection format

When a step runs on a **remote host**, print **one copy-pasteable line** — never “SSH to the server” without the full command.

## Template

```bash
ssh -i ~/.ssh/7-5-25kuroit joshfialkoff@HOST 'REMOTE_COMMAND'
```

- **Key:** `~/.ssh/7-5-25kuroit`
- **User:** `joshfialkoff` (use `opencode` only when docs/scripts explicitly require it for deploy)
- **HOST:** pick the correct origin (see below)
- **REMOTE_COMMAND:** the exact command to run there (quote for single-line copy-paste)

## Hosts (this repo)

| Host | When |
|------|------|
| `104.168.38.162` | **Current production** (Traefik, `/opt/assistedly`, `cloudflared`, Docker deploy) |
| `75.127.14.185` | **Migration target** (Dify co-located nginx host; use when runbooks say dify-host) |

Default to **`104.168.38.162`** unless the task is explicitly about the Dify migration host.

## Examples

Production — restart tunnel connector:

```bash
ssh -i ~/.ssh/7-5-25kuroit joshfialkoff@104.168.38.162 'sudo systemctl start cloudflared'
```

Production — inspect app container:

```bash
ssh -i ~/.ssh/7-5-25kuroit joshfialkoff@104.168.38.162 'docker compose -p assistedlyai ps'
```

Migration host — example remote command:

```bash
ssh -i ~/.ssh/7-5-25kuroit joshfialkoff@75.127.14.185 'docker ps --format "{{.Names}}"'
```

## Local vs remote

- **In this Cursor workspace on your Mac:** `npm run dev`, `npm run build`, etc. — no SSH wrapper.
- **On the origin server:** always use the full `ssh -i … joshfialkoff@HOST '…'` form above.
